source: crates/engage/tests/integrations/main.rs
description: Should successfully print the long help and exit.
---
A process composer with ordering and parallelism based on directed acyclic graphs.

Usage: engage [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  just         Run a specific process
  dot          Output Graphviz' `dot` representation of the DAG and exit
  list         Print a list of the available processes
  completions  Print completions for a given shell
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -f, --file <FILE>
          Manually choose the Engage file.
          
          This overrides the default searching behavior. Processes will still be spawned with the parent directory of the chosen file as their current working directory.

  -l, --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          Log format.
          
          By default this uses Engage's custom log format which is optimal for regular usage. Other log formats are implemented by [`tracing_subscriber`] and also respect the `RUST_LOG` environment variable; these formats are primarily useful for debugging.

          Possible values:
          - default: The default format
          - compact: [`tracing_subscriber`]'s compact format
          - full:    [`tracing_subscriber`]'s full format
          - pretty:  [`tracing_subscriber`]'s pretty format
          - json:    [`tracing_subscriber`]'s JSON format
          
          [default: default]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
